//-->
    </script>I wonder if there shouldn't be a license that wouldn't allow people to feed the code to LLMs.    <script type="text/javascript">      
<!--
        document.write('</div>');      
//-->
    </script>  </div></blockquote>
<br />
I'm sure that's something that will come out of this, but I suspect it will be ignored. &quot;AI&quot; pushers, from the model developers to the end users, operate on the assumption that they're entitled to just do whatever they want, and they'll go <i>way</i> past source-code license violations (look at how much violation of actual legally-enforceable copyrights they've already done.)
<br />

<br />
My long-term hope is that, once the money firehose funding this stuff dries up and it becomes economically impossible to operate at scale, this kind of thing goes away - but <i>boy</i> do I wish we could just skip straight to that part :/<br />
